=== Prompt ===
Who is Frida Kahlo?

=== Response ===
Frida Kahlo (1907-1954) was a renowned Mexican painter known for her self-portraits and works that explored themes of identity, post-colonialism, gender, class, and race in Mexican society. Her work is celebrated for its pain and passion, and its intense, dense imagery. Kahlo's paintings are often deeply personal, drawing from her own life experiences, including a debilitating bus accident that left her with lifelong physical pain and multiple surgeries.

Kahlo was born in Coyoacán, a neighborhood in Mexico City, to a German immigrant father and a Mexican mother of indigenous and Spanish ancestry. She had a tumultuous marriage with the famous Mexican muralist Diego Rivera, whom she met when she was 18 and he was 42. Their relationship was marked by both love and intense conflict.

Despite enduring numerous health issues throughout her life, Kahlo continued to paint and explore her unique artistic vision. Her work gained international recognition in the late 20th century, and today, she is considered one of the most significant figures in 20th-century art. Her legacy extends beyond her paintings; she has become an iconic figure for women and those who identify as LGBTQ+, due to her strength, resilience, and her open expression of her identity and experiences.

Her life story has been adapted into several films, books, and documentaries, ensuring her influence continues to be felt across various cultural and artistic domains.

